{
  "dom_id": "question-166289",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "What is the average rate of change of the function $f(x)$ over the interval $x\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}+h],$ where $h>0$ is a parameter? Express your answer in terms of $h.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\frac{\u0394f}{\u0394x}\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "We have the function $f(x)=5sin\u2061(2x).$ Notice that we are given the length $h$ of the interval. So, the average rate of change of $f$ over this interval is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u0394f}{\u0394x}=\\frac{f(a+h)-f(a)}{h},\n$$\n\nwith $a=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Substituting into the formula and simplifying gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u0394f}{\u0394x} & =\\frac{f(a+h)-f(a)}{h} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+h)-f(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{h} \\\\  & =\\frac{5sin\u2061(2(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+h))-5sin\u2061(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})}{h} \\\\  & =\\frac{5sin\u2061(\\pi +2h)-5sin\u2061(\\pi )}{h} \\\\  & =\\frac{5sin\u2061(\\pi +2h)-5(0)}{h} \\\\  & =\\frac{5sin\u2061(\\pi +2h)}{h} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{h}sin\u2061(\\pi +2h).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
